/-!
# Explicit derived-series obstructions in seven-point overgroups

There are 98 double cosets of the standard even Sylow subgroup in S₇.
For each representative outside both source partition stabilizers, short words
x, y, z satisfy x ≠ 1 and x = z [x, y x y⁻¹] z⁻¹. Normality of the derived
series puts x in every derived subgroup, contradicting solvability.
The words and their equations are checked by the kernel; no subgroup catalogue
or solvability decision procedure is assumed. `Coverage` proves that the
representatives exhaust S₇.

Source: Aschbacher–Smith, *The Classification of Quasithin Groups*,
13.8.24, printed pp.958–959 (1 March 2004 manuscript).
-/

@[expose] public section
open Equiv Subgroup
open scoped commutatorElement
namespace CFSG.Quasithin.Chapter13.Section08.ComponentSieve.Seven.LocalGeometry.PermutationOvergroups.PlacementCertificate

